# Build context for tests/install/Dockerfile.ubuntu1804, which copies the repo
# in and builds it from source. The context needs the tracked source tree and
# nothing else. On a clean CI checkout that is already nearly true; on a working
# machine the untracked output dwarfs it — 31 GB here when this file was written
# — and the documented `docker build` would sit copying it instead of building.
#
# `.git` is deliberately NOT excluded: rust/crates/cli/build.rs stamps the
# binary via `git rev-parse`, and without it `camdl --version` reports
# "unknown", which is the one thing this test asserts.

# Build output. Regenerated inside the image, and a host build must not leak in:
# an amd64 image carrying an arm64 binary would pass without building anything.
rust/target/
target/
ocaml/_build/
_build/

# Agent worktrees and local scratch.
.claude/
results/
review-zips/
tb-household-probe/

# Generated fit/validation data under the external-validation corpus. Its
# tracked files are the case definitions, a few hundred KB; the rest is output.
# The image only runs `make build` and `make install`, never the suite.
tests/external/runs/
tests/external/cases/*/results/
